  "notes": "gbdraw: a local scientific web app (Tailwind slate/blue palette) that renders GenBank genome diagrams. Left panel is a dense parameter sidebar with a 13-icon section-jump bar, white rounded cards, small clock-ish 'Applies on Generate' markers beside each section title, and a large sticky blue 'Generate Diagram' button at the panel bottom. Header packs tiny 11px bordered utility buttons (Reset/Save/Load Session) beside a single filled blue 'Gallery & tutorials' CTA, and a pill segmented Circular/Linear mode switch. Preview area: rounded white card with export buttons (SVG, Interactive SVG, PNG, PDF), floating feature-search bar (regex, prev/next, open), and a bottom floating toolbar (Reset Layout, Layout edit, Canvas padding, Search, zoom +/−, 39%, Fit). Diagram is a multi-genome synteny plot with salmon-pink identity ribbons. A dark right-edge tab opens an Editor drawer. The provided first-viewport image shows an empty state ('Open Gallery example' / 'Learn with tutorials' over a dashed drop area) while the capture shows a loaded session; label follows the capture. Language selector with 17 locales and a translation-feedback link."
}
